## NS1 — LLM-anchored text encoder (in progress)

*Started 2026-05-13. Major plan refinement + infra fix + Novelty A: 2026-06-11.*

Replaces the frozen-CLIP text anchor with a stronger external semantic prior (a frozen sentence transformer / LLM). Acts on CLIP's text encoder via a small projection MLP + cosine drift loss on the Conceptual Captions reference pool.

### Implementation status (as of 2026-06-11)
- `mtil/src/models/llm_anchor.py` — projection head, embedding precompute + disk cache, cosine loss, per-task projection persistence. **Encoder/decoder auto-detection** (encoder: mean-pool; decoder LLMs containing `qwen`/`llama`/`mistral`/`gpt`/`falcon`/`phi` in name: last-token pool). Auto-sets pad token from EOS for decoder models.
- `mtil/phase3/args_phase3.py` — `--lambda_llm_anchor`, `--llm_anchor_model` (default `intfloat/e5-large-v2`), `--llm_anchor_hidden` (default 768), `--llm_anchor_batch_size` (default 64).
- `mtil/phase3/trainer_phase3.py` — loss term (6), wired into the existing 5-loss Phase 3 loop.
- `mtil/scripts/prestage_hf_anchor.sh` — login-node HF download helper. Defaults to `intfloat/e5-large-v2`; override via `HF_MODELS` env var.
- `mtil/scripts/11task/llm_anchor_lam03.sh` — NS1-additive launcher (e5-large-v2, λ_anchor=0.3, 72h H100-3g.40gb).
- `mtil/scripts/11task/llm_anchor_smoke.sh` — 250-iter smoke test on Aircraft. **Note:** must be ≥ warmup_length to avoid `ZeroDivisionError` in `src/utils.py:28` LR scheduler (`es = steps - warmup_length` divides by zero when equal). Pre-existing bug; production runs (1500+ iters) clear warmup safely.
- `mtil/scripts/11task/llm_anchor_no_zscl_text.sh` — drop-ZSCL-text ablation launcher (omits `--text_loss`). On stacked branch `llm-anchor-no-zscl-text`.

### Refined ablation grid

LLM only anchors text (no image encoder in the LLM). So **dropping ZSCL image** removes anti-drift signal that NS1 doesn't replace — image-side ZSCL must stay. The headline ablation is drop-text only; drop-all is a control.

| Variant | L_L2 | L_ZSCL-image | L_ZSCL-text | L_RTD | L_LLM_anchor | Total | Status / role |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Phase 3 (v4) | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | 5 | base (done) |
| NS1-additive (lam03) | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | 6 | **submitted (job 15969984)** |
| **NS1-drop-text-ZSCL** | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | 5 | **submitted (job 15970119)** — headline |
| NS1-drop-all-ZSCL | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | 4 | control (not yet built) |
| NS1-drop-L2 | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | 5 | optional (not yet built) |
| NS1-minimal | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | 4 | optional (not yet built) |

**Killer result framing:** if **NS1-drop-text-ZSCL ≥ Phase 3**, the thesis story becomes *"a single stronger anchor replaces the weaker text-side ZSCL anchor — simpler method, same or better numbers."* That's a much cleaner contribution than "+1 loss."

**No new CLI flags needed.** Existing args provide full ablation granularity:
- Drop ZSCL text → omit `--text_loss`
- Drop ZSCL image → omit `--image_loss`
- Drop L_L2 → `--l2 0` (gated at `trainer_phase3.py:457`)

